@Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5276

# Requests for the mock wallet, against the frozen seed (data/seed/README.md). The contract is docs/wallet-api.md.
# User 1 (07805550001) is the demo user and users 1 to 5 exist; 07805550101 is Hammoudi (contact S01 of user 1, not a user);
# bill account 1 is user 1's home electricity; product 1 is Zain credit 5,000.
# Change @idempotencyKey before each new payment: a used key replays the stored outcome instead of paying again.
# Keys are 1 to 64 characters of A-Z, a-z, 0-9, _ and -; anything else is 400 invalid_idempotency_key.
@idempotencyKey = http-demo-001

# Every /admin request carries the X-Wallet-Admin-Key header. In Development with no Wallet:AdminKey set, any non-empty
# value is accepted (the header is there so a browser must preflight). With a key set, put the key here instead.
@adminKey = dev

### Health
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/health

### One user
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1

### User 5 gives consent (204; again is also 204; a reset clears it)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/5/consent

### The wallet account behind a phone number (registered name and status, active or closed)
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/accounts/by-phone/07805550101

### Contacts and aliases of user 1 (add ?q= to filter by a substring of the saved name or alias)
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/contacts

### Bills of user 1
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/bills

### Balance of user 1
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/balance

### History of user 1: transfers to Hammoudi, newest first
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/history?to=07805550101&take=10

### Store catalogue: Zain credit cards
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/store/products?provider=Zain&type=credit

### Orders of user 1
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/orders

### Quote: 50,000 to Hammoudi (no money moves)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "transfer",
  "amountIqd": 50000,
  "toPhone": "07805550101"
}

### Quote: pay bill account 1 in full
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "bill",
  "billAccountId": 1
}

### Execute: 50,000 to Hammoudi (201 the first time, 200 replay with the same key)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "transfer",
  "amountIqd": 50000,
  "toPhone": "07805550101"
}

### Execute: pay bill account 1 (amount comes from the wallet)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}-bill

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "bill",
  "billAccountId": 1
}

### Execute: buy product 1 (the response carries the purchase code)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}-purchase

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "purchase",
  "productId": 1
}

### Look up the transfer by its key
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions/by-key/{{idempotencyKey}}

### Current fault switch
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Fault: the next execute waits 300 ms, then runs normally
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "mode": "slow",
  "delayMs": 300,
  "once": true
}

### Fault: the next execute commits, then hangs for the configured delay (look it up by key meanwhile)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "mode": "timeoutAfterExecute",
  "once": true
}

### Clear the fault switch
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "mode": "none"
}

### Reset: restore the seed exactly and clear faults
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/reset
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
